---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import {legacyWorks} from '../lib/legacy-works';
import {url} from '../lib/content';
---
<Page title="Earlier studies" description="Where the earlier Animatix demos went, and what to use instead.">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Archive / not the current collection</p><h1>Keep the history.<br/><em>Choose what comes next.</em></h1><p class="lead">These nine studies helped develop Animatix. They are no longer presented as finished public work. Their sources remain available, with the limitations recorded rather than hidden.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('showcase/')}>Browse current work →</a></section>
  <div class="lessons">{legacyWorks.map((work,i)=><a href={url(`demos/${work.id}/`)}><span class="lesson-number">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h2>{work.title}</h2><p>{work.decision}</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>)}</div>
  <section class="note"><h2>Source preservation is not a quality badge.</h2><p>Archived scenes can still exercise useful engine behaviour. Their existence in the repository does not mean every explanation, parameter setting or layout is suitable for publication.</p></section>
</Page>
